{
  "name" : "Hoffmann2002_KnockOut_IkBNFkB_Signaling",
  "description" : "<notes xmlns=\"http://www.sbml.org/sbml/level2\">      <body xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">        <p>The model corresponds to the knock out model of beta-/-, epsilon -/- and reproduces the upper panel in Fig 2C. In order to reproduce the other knock out models the transcription rate of the species that are not present must be set to zero and the rate of the one that is present must be set as seven times its corresponding value for the wild type model. This is done so as to compensate for the loss of other isoforms.  Model was successfully tested on MathSBML.</p>            <br />            <p>To the extent possible under law, all copyright and related or neighbouring rights to this encoded model have been dedicated to the public domain worldwide. Please refer to      <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\" title=\"Creative Commons CC0\">CC0 Public Domain Dedication</a>          for more information.      </p>            <p>In summary, you are entitled to use this encoded model in absolutely any manner you deem suitable, verbatim, or with modification, alone or embedded it in a larger context, redistribute it, commercially or not, in a restricted way or not.</p>            <br />            <p>To cite BioModels Database, please use:      <a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20587024\" target=\"_blank\">Li C, Donizelli M, Rodriguez N, Dharuri H, Endler L, Chelliah V, Li L, He E, Henry A, Stefan MI, Snoep JL, Hucka M, Le Novère N, Laibe C (2010) BioModels Database: An enhanced, curated and annotated resource for published quantitative kinetic models. BMC Syst Biol., 4:92.</a>                </p>            </body>          </notes>",
  "format" : {
